cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spectrAccess, please cite it as below."
title: "spectrAccess"
authors:
  - name: "SpectraWorks B.V."
version: "0.6.0" # x-release-please-version
license: "Apache-2.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpectraWorksOSS/SpectrAccess"
abstract: "spectrAccess is one Python interface for Earth observation satellite data and the reference measurements used to calibrate and validate it. It finds and downloads satellite imagery, mostly Level-1 (Sentinel-2, Sentinel-3, Landsat, VIIRS, MTG FCI, MSG SEVIRI, EMIT), and calibration and atmospheric reference data (RadCalNet, GSICS, AERONET, CAMS, Sentinel-3 OLCI water vapour, GNSS) as each provider publishes them, keeping provider metadata, and uncertainty where the provider publishes it. It does not correct or calibrate the data."
keywords:
  - earth observation
  - remote sensing
  - satellite data access
  - calibration and validation
  - radiometric calibration
  - Sentinel-2
  - Landsat
  - RadCalNet
  - GSICS
  - AERONET

